# ============================================================================
# FlowAblation / 1D Stefan problem  (Hydro2, ablation.on = 1, non-deforming embedded solid)
#
# Gas at rest (rho 1, p 1, gamma 1.4, cp 3.5, cv 2.5 -> T = p/(rho (cp - cv)) = 1; mu 1e-3,
# Pr 0.72 -> k = mu cp/Pr = 4.861e-3, alpha = k/(rho cp) = 1.389e-3) fills x > 0.3 against a
# solid wall held at the ablation temperature T_w = 0.9.  The heat conducted into the wall
# removes solid: rho_s Q* ds/dt = q_w (ablation.rho_s = 1, ablation.Qstar = 1.757).
# One-phase Stefan similarity solution (constant properties, gas motion neglected):
#   surface position   x_s = 0.3 - s,  s = 2 lam sqrt(alpha t)
#   lam exp(lam^2) (1 + erf lam) = rho cp (T_inf - T_w)/(sqrt(pi) rho_s Q*)   ->  lam = 0.100
#   T(x, t) = T_w + (T_inf - T_w) (erf((x - 0.3)/(2 sqrt(alpha t))) + erf lam)/(1 + erf lam)
#   q_w = k (T_inf - T_w) exp(-lam^2)/((1 + erf lam) sqrt(pi alpha t))
# At t = 7.2: s = 0.0200 (8 cells of the 400).  The solution neglects the O(lam), O(dT/T)
# flow of gas into the vacated layer and its density change, so expect a few per cent.
#
# Run (from bin/): mpirun -np 4 ./hydro2-2d-g++ ../tests/FlowAblation/input_1D_Stefan plot_file=<dir>/output
# Check:           python3 ../tests/FlowAblation/reference/stefan_check.py <dir>
# ============================================================================
